{"kind":"charness.bounded_review.v1","lens":"release lock-in final pass","verdict":"block","target_observations":null,"findings":[{"id":"R-004","severity":"low","summary":"The docs summary can imply that the second due check stops the lane even when a young command defers the sequence.","evidence":["docs/agent-task-runs.md says “a second due check, deferred while a young command runs, stops it.”","The spec says that when a young command defers the request at a due check, the next empty due check delivers the request, and the stop waits one more check. That next check does not stop the lane."],"action":"Clarify that the second empty due check stops only when the request was already delivered; when a young command defers the sequence, the next due check delivers the request and a later empty check stops."}],"counterweight_triage":[{"concern":"R-003: snapshot work can delay later checks, so a hard wall-clock bound is not established.","bin":"fixed","disposition":"The spec names the live snapshot as work that delays the next check and explicitly states that windows are nominal and it gives no hard wall-clock bound."},{"concern":"R-004: release notes and docstring still describe a fixed extra window.","bin":"fixed","disposition":"The notes say deferral is by one more check and explain that windows are nominal; the docstring also says deferral is by one check and that windows are nominal."},{"concern":"R-004: docs summary describes stop timing under young-command deferral.","bin":"block","disposition":"The summary’s second-due-check wording is ambiguous in a way that can lead readers to expect a stop before the request is delivered."}],"next_move":"Clarify the docs summary’s due-check sequence, then repeat the bounded review.","non_claims":["Reviewed the identity-bound inline payload; did not inspect workspace paths or run tests.","Did not independently verify unrelated release-note claims."]}
